@startuml

' Turn initiation flow
GE -> UI: Push [Current Player Turn Start] notification
UI --> P: Display turn start screen, prompt for action
P -> UI: Confirm to start turn
UI -> GE: Trigger turn initialization

' Turn initialization: Draw cards + reset state
GE -> CM: Execute turn start draw (Default 2 cards)
CM -> PM: Add drawn cards to player's hand
GE -> PM: Reset player turn state (Remaining actions = 3)
PM --> GE: Return updated player state
GE -> UM: Trigger UI refresh
UM --> UI: Update player hand, action count, turn info
UI --> P: Display turn action interface

' Loop for in-turn actions (matches course loop standard)
loop Remaining actions > 0 AND Player has not ended turn
    P -> UI: Select in-turn action
    UI -> GE: Submit player action command

    ' Branch: Player chooses to play card OR end turn
    alt Player selects [Play Card] action
        ' Reuse Play Card use case (matches UML reuse standard)
        ref over P,UI,GE,GRV,CM,PM,UM : Play Card Use Case
    else Player selects [End Turn]
        break ' Exit loop, end turn actions
    end
end

' End-of-turn hand validation: Max 7 cards (per game rules)
GE -> GRV: Validate player hand count compliance (≤7 cards)
GRV --> GE: Return validation result
alt Hand count > 7, must discard
    UI --> P: Prompt [Must discard to ≤7 cards]
    ' Loop discard until compliant
    loop Player hand count > 7
        P -> UI: Select card to discard
        UI -> GE: Submit discard request
        GE -> CM: Execute discard processing
        CM -> PM: Remove card from hand, add to discard pile
        GE -> UM: Refresh hand display
    end
end

' Turn wrap-up
GE -> GE: Mark current player turn ended
GE -> GE: Switch to next player
GE -> UM: Trigger global UI update
UM --> UI: Display turn end screen, switch to next player
UI --> P: Prompt [Turn ended]
@enduml